WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.210
A fraction always means a fraction of something.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.650
Half of a whole bar is six squares.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.610
Half of what is left is only three squares.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.050
Same fraction, different whole, different amount.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:15.830
Before using any fraction, say what it is a fraction of.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.050
This matters most when things change in stages.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.540
A second fraction or percentage usually applies to the

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.170
new amount, not the original.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.390
Forgetting that is the classic trap.

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:29.220
A jar holds forty marbles.

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.340
Ali takes one quarter of them.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.920
Then Bea takes one third of what remains.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:35.680
How many marbles are left?

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.120
Pause and name the whole for each fraction.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:45.590
Ali's quarter is a quarter of forty, which is ten.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:47.270
Thirty marbles remain.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.980
Bea's third is a third of thirty, not of forty.

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:52.500
That is ten more.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.140
Twenty marbles are left.

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:57.300
A third of the original forty would split a marble,

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:00.070
a clue that we have used the wrong whole.

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:02.420
A grid shows a fraction of a fraction.

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:05.120
Shade three of four columns: three quarters.

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:08.020
Then take two of the three rows of that part:

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:09.920
two thirds of three quarters.

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:12.660
The overlap is six cells out of twelve,

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:14.020
which is one half.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:16.620
To find a fraction of a fraction, multiply.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:19.090
Now the price trap.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.820
A one hundred dollar item goes up by ten percent,

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:22.770
to one hundred and ten.

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:25.620
Then it goes down by ten percent.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:28.150
Ten percent of one hundred and ten is eleven,

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.130
so the price becomes ninety-nine.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:33.560
The two changes do not cancel, because they are

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.740
percentages of different wholes.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:38.170
Always ask: fraction of what?

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:40.510
Update the whole after each step.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.890
Notebook challenge: a tank is full.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:46.380
One fifth is used on Monday, and one quarter of the

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:47.370
remainder on Tuesday.

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:49.550
What fraction of the tank is left?
